From 3b7ea14cf75c8c951ffe13e64d13440f5db8adac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:29:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): skip walled reviews at pickup and bound deferral
 events [daveey]

Problem: a pickup worker copied walled review cards every tick (16 imports
in 8 ticks) and starved a pinned eligible card; two workers with different
wall deadlines appended one review_route_deferred event per sync cycle.

Why 1: _evaluate had no pre-copy check for review_provider_wall, unlike
quota_held/paced. Evidence: deleting the _review_walled call reopens 16
imports / 8 ticks.
Why 2: hold wrote review_route_deferred, not respawn_guarded, so
board_hold did not treat the card as already held. Pickup then spent
budget copying it.
Why 3: de-dupe compared only the newest payload with this host's
{reason, until}; two hosts with different deadlines always appended.
Evidence: newest-only mutant grows 24 events over 12 cycles; unique
payloads stay at 2.
Why 4: _tick_skips listed named result buckets and start_gate.word
ignores review_provider_wall, so ready-wait notices read skip_unrecorded.

Root (happened): the new pre-claim hold was not wired into pickup's
pre-copy pattern or the skip/event cross-host bound.
Root (not caught): original regressions were single-host dispatch only;
no two-gateway pickup or two-deadline event test.

Countermeasures:
- pickup_hold + _review_walled before copy (quota_hold skip, fail open)
- append review_route_deferred only when that payload is new on the card
- record dispatch_skipped from clock_held so notices name the wall

Proof: 40 admission/pickup tests green; three mutants red; 201 consumer
tests; scripts/check 21 green.
